  {
   "@id": "http://localhost:8080/how-much-do-movers-cost-in-san-diego/#faq",
   "@type": "FAQPage",
   "mainEntity": [
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Movers generally refuse hazardous materials such as gasoline, propane tanks, paint, aerosols and cleaning chemicals, along with perishable food, plants and pets. Most also ask you to carry cash, jewelry and important papers yourself. Ask each company for its list before you pack, so nothing left behind on moving day adds a second trip to how much do movers cost in San Diego."
     },
     "name": "What items won't San Diego movers take on the truck?"
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Tipping is up to you. Many guides suggest 10% to 20% of the bill, shared among the crew, or $10.00–$20.00 per mover for a job of up to 4 hours. The tip calculator on this page works out both, and the tip comes on top of how much do movers cost in San Diego on the bill."
     },
     "name": "How much should you tip on a San Diego move of a few hundred dollars?"
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Each company sets its own hourly rate, minimum hours, base fee and travel charges, and some estimate the hours more honestly than others. A busy market like San Diego's widens the gaps between companies. Compare totals made after a visual inspection, not hourly rates alone, and hold them against the calculator's range for how much do movers cost in San Diego."
     },
     "name": "Why do San Diego moving quotes differ so much for the same home?"
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Los Angeles is about 120 road miles from San Diego, past California's 100-mile line, so the move is charged by weight and mileage rather than by the hour. It costs more than a move across town but well below a 1,000-mile move, which runs $2,600–$5,700 for a 2-bedroom home off peak. Enter both ZIP codes in the calculator to see how much do movers cost in San Diego for that route."
     },
     "name": "How much do movers cost in San Diego for a move to Los Angeles?"
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "The common ones are a base fee before the hourly billing starts, a minimum number of hours, stairs, a long carry or a shuttle truck where the big truck can't park, and packing materials. A building's move-in fee is separate again. Ask for every charge in writing before moving day."
     },
     "name": "What extra charges show up on San Diego moving bills?"
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
